From: Comzee <117947104+Comzee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: rockchip: describe RK3128 QoS priorities

Describe the optional high/low priority pair used by the RK312x BSP for
external NoC ports. The power-domain controller owns initialization and
save/restore of these syscon registers.

Signed-off-by: Comzee <117947104+Comzee@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/rockchip/rockchip,rk3128-qos.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/rockchip/rockchip,rk3128-qos.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..44a51ce
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/rockchip/rockchip,rk3128-qos.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/soc/rockchip/rockchip,rk3128-qos.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Rockchip RK3128 interconnect QoS port
+
+maintainers:
+  - Heiko Stuebner <heiko@sntech.de>
+
+description: |
+  Per-master NoC QoS registers. The power-domain controller saves and restores
+  these registers through its pm_qos phandles. An optional board priority is
+  initialized while the domain is powered and reapplied after power-on.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    items:
+      - const: rockchip,rk3128-qos
+      - const: syscon
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  rockchip,priority:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+    description: High and low priority levels, as in the RK312x vendor binding.
+    items:
+      - maximum: 3
+      - maximum: 3
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    qos@1012f180 {
+        compatible = "rockchip,rk3128-qos", "syscon";
+        reg = <0x1012f180 0x20>;
+        rockchip,priority = <3 3>;
+    };
